{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>She is more righteous than I.</b> What is <b>than I</b>? Rather, HaShem says: that she did — to come to me, to raise up seed for the deceased, from me. And not from Shelah, for he feared lest his seed be corrupted like his brothers and die." "<b>For therefore.</b> For behold, on account of this — that I feared lest his seed be corrupted and die like his brothers — I did not give her to Shelah my son. Another interpretation: <b>She is more righteous than I</b> — from me she merited; it is justice that I not judge her guilty, for if I held her liable I would be holding myself liable." "<b>And he did not add again to know her.</b> And he did not cease from coming to her, for at first he came to her for the purpose of levirate consummation, לדעתה, as we said above. And some say: in that generation they would betroth only by intercourse, and betrothal by intercourse effects kiddushin only for one who is penetrated in the normal manner, but Er and Onan who used her not in the normal manner — therefore she was not his daughter-in-law. Another interpretation: <b>And he did not add</b> — he did not continue, thinking she is akatlanit (a woman whose husbands die). Another interpretation: he was ashamed, for she was his daughter-in-law. And if you interpret it as 'he did not cease,' he should not have written לדעתה, but rather מדעתה (with her consent)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:59.834554202Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}